-- title:
--   Geometric integrality of the two-chart model over ℤ[1/N]
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number, let $F_N =$ `modularFunctionFieldFull N` be the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\mathbb{Q}$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ generated by the set of all $q$-expansions $\mathrm{qExpand}\,\mathbb{Q}\,d\,j_q$ for nonzero divisors $d$ of $N$, and let `IgusaScheme.jFull N` be the element $j_q$ of $F_N$. Form the two-chart integral model [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) over $\mathbb{Z}$ attached to the data $(\mathbb{Z}, F_N, j_q)$, namely the pushout of the two morphisms $\mathrm{Spec}$ applied to the inclusions of the finite and infinite chart rings into the middle ring, together with its structure morphism `toBase` to $\mathrm{Spec}\,\mathbb{Z}$. Its base change `baseChange` along $\mathbb{Z} \to \mathrm{Localization.Away}\,(N : \mathbb{Z}) = \mathbb{Z}[1/N]$, i.e. the fibre product of `toBase` with $\mathrm{Spec}(\mathbb{Z}[1/N]) \to \mathrm{Spec}\,\mathbb{Z}$, comes with the second projection `baseChangeToBase` to $\mathrm{Spec}(\mathbb{Z}[1/N])$. The assertion is that this projection is geometrically integral in Mathlib's sense: for every field $K$, every morphism $\mathrm{Spec}\,K \to \mathrm{Spec}(\mathbb{Z}[1/N])$ and every pullback square over it, the resulting scheme $Z$ is an integral scheme.
--
--   This records that the two-chart integral model of $X_0(N)$ built from the $q$-expansions $j(q^d)$, $d \mid N$, has geometrically integral fibres over the good-reduction base $\mathbb{Z}[1/N]$. It is used downstream in the construction of Deligne–Rapoport-style model packages, in the integrality statement for the structure morphism over $\mathbb{Z}$ with $N$ invertible, and in the Abel–Jacobi/relative-group-law constructions on these curves.
